H("681.d.4.F",4,"UDP is considered connectionless because it:","sends data without first setting up a connection",["always checks every packet","needs a handshake","guarantees delivery"],"UDP skips setup.")
H("681.d.4.G",3,"The ping utility uses which protocol to test connectivity?","ICMP",["HTTP","SMTP","FTP"],"Ping sends ICMP echo messages.")
H("681.d.4.G",4,"Which tool shows the route packets take to a destination?","traceroute",["notepad","paint","defrag"],"Traceroute lists hops.")
H("681.d.4.H",3,"A technician can validate a local network card is working by pinging:","the loopback address 127.0.0.1",["the moon","a random website only","the printer toner"],"The loopback tests the TCP/IP stack.")
H("681.d.4.H",4,"If pinging an IP address works but pinging a website name fails, the likely problem is with:","name resolution (DNS)",["the monitor","the keyboard","the power cord"],"DNS translates names to addresses.")
H("681.d.4.I",3,"Which practice improves network security?","using strong passwords and updates",["sharing passwords","disabling firewalls","leaving defaults"],"Basic hygiene reduces risk.")
H("681.d.4.I",4,"Changing the default router password is important because defaults are:","publicly known to attackers",["too long","unneeded","easy to forget"],"Default credentials are widely published.")
H("681.d.5.A",3,"Comparing a star network with a ring network is an example of:","analyzing types of networks",["baking","painting","gardening"],"Analysis compares features.")
H("681.d.5.A",4,"A network component that connects the local network to the internet is the:","router",["keyboard","mouse","speaker"],"Routers link networks to the internet.")
H("681.d.5.B",3,"A busy office with many users probably needs a network with more:","bandwidth",["decorations","windows","chairs"],"More users need more capacity.")
H("681.d.5.B",4,"When choosing between wired and wireless for a fixed desktop that needs a stable fast link, a technician would likely pick:","wired Ethernet",["wireless always","no network","dial-up"],"Wired is often steadier and faster.")
H("681.d.6.A",3,"Before building a network, planning documents should show the:","layout, equipment and cable paths",["lunch menu","vacation days","pet policy"],"Plans guide the build.")
H("681.d.6.A",4,"A bill of materials for a network project lists:","all parts to be purchased and their quantities",["employees' birthdays","office plants","parking permits"],"BOMs support ordering.")
H("681.d.6.B",3,"Heat can affect network equipment by:","causing devices to fail or slow down",["making them faster","cleaning them","adding memory"],"Overheating damages equipment.")
H("681.d.6.B",4,"Which environmental factor can cause interference with unshielded network cables?","nearby electrical motors or fluorescent lights",["a quiet hallway","a coat rack","a painted wall"],"Electrical noise interferes with signals.")
H("681.d.6.C",3,"An Ethernet port on a computer is also called a:","LAN port",["USB drive","HDMI cable","audio mix"],"It connects to the LAN.")
H("681.d.6.C",4,"A device that connects several computers and passes traffic between their ports is a:","switch",["monitor","scanner","microphone"],"Switches connect multiple hosts.")
H("681.d.6.D",3,"A subnetting chart lists the:","address ranges for each subnet",["employee salaries","paint colors","parking spots"],"The chart organizes subnet ranges.")
H("681.d.6.D",4,"A subnet mask of 255.255.255.0 means the first three parts of the address identify the:","network",["host only","user name","printer"],"The mask separates network from host.")
H("681.d.6.E",3,"A cable tester is used to:","check that a cable is wired correctly",["measure room size","play music","print documents"],"Testers check continuity and wiring.")
H("681.d.6.E",4,"A crimping tool is used to:","attach connectors to cable ends",["cut wood","paint walls","measure voltage"],"Crimpers fasten RJ-45 plugs.")
H("681.d.6.F",3,"A patch is a:","small update that fixes a problem in software",["type of cable","kind of router","screen cover"],"Patches fix bugs.")
H("681.d.6.F",4,"Before applying a vendor fix to a production network device, a technician should read the:","release notes and test if possible",["advertisement","menu","calendar"],"Notes describe changes and risks.")
H("681.d.6.G",3,"A backup copy kept off-site helps protect data from:","fire or theft at the main location",["slow typing","a dirty screen","a loose chair"],"Off-site copies survive local disasters.")
H("681.d.6.G",4,"A common good practice is to follow the 3-2-1 rule, which means keeping:","three copies on two kinds of media with one off-site",["one copy in one place","two copies on one drive","no copies"],"3-2-1 spreads risk.")
H("681.d.6.H",3,"Which can slow a network?","too many users sharing limited bandwidth",["a quiet room","a short cable","a new switch"],"Congestion reduces speed.")
H("681.d.6.H",4,"A very long cable run beyond the standard distance limit can cause:","signal loss and errors",["faster speeds","stronger signals","no change"],"Distance weakens signals.")
H("681.d.7.A",3,"A recovery plan for a network should state how to restore:","critical services and data after an outage",["office music","vending machines","parking lots"],"Plans focus on restoring operations.")
H("681.d.7.A",4,"In a recovery plan, the most important systems are usually restored:","first",["last","never","at random"],"Critical systems are prioritized.")
H("681.d.7.B",3,"A maintenance plan for network devices might schedule:","firmware updates and cable checks",["office parties","paint jobs","furniture moves"],"Planned upkeep prevents failures.")
H("681.d.7.B",4,"Keeping a maintenance log helps the team:","see what was done and when",["hide tasks","avoid planning","skip checks"],"Logs track maintenance history.")
H("682.d.1.A",3,"A telecommunications technician who is dependable and shows initiative is more likely to:","keep their job and move up",["lose their badge","be ignored","get fewer tasks"],"Strong work habits support advancement.")
H("682.d.1.A",4,"Which is a work behavior employers value in a cable installer?","completing jobs on schedule with attention to detail",["rushing sloppy work","skipping safety checks","arriving whenever convenient"],"Quality and timeliness matter.")
H("682.d.1.B",3,"A person who adjusts easily when job plans change shows:","flexibility",["stubbornness","indifference","carelessness"],"Flexibility helps in changing work.")
H("682.d.1.B",4,"Open-mindedness during a team troubleshooting session means you:","listen to others' theories before deciding",["dismiss all ideas","talk over teammates","refuse to test anything"],"Open-minded teams find causes faster.")
H("682.d.1.C",3,"A network installer reading the wiring standard before starting is:","using reading skills to prevent errors",["wasting time","delaying the job","ignoring the work order"],"Reading prevents mistakes.")
H("682.d.1.C",4,"A well-written incident report should state:","what happened, when and what was done",["opinions only","jokes","a guess of blame"],"Reports must be factual.")
H("682.d.1.D",3,"Speaking clearly to a client about an outage and when it will be fixed shows:","good verbal communication",["poor planning","laziness","rudeness"],"Clear speech informs the client.")
H("682.d.1.D",4,"A technician crosses their arms, frowns and looks away while a client explains a problem. This nonverbal signal suggests:","disinterest",["careful listening","agreement","excitement"],"Body language can signal attitude.")
H("682.d.1.E",3,"A network is slow. A good first problem-solving step is to:","identify when and where the slowdown happens",["buy new equipment","blame the users","restart everything blindly"],"Defining the problem comes first.")
H("682.d.1.E",4,"Critical thinking during troubleshooting includes:","forming a theory and testing it",["assuming the first guess","skipping tests","copying someone else's answer"],"Theories need testing.")
H("682.d.1.F",3,"On a cable installation crew, leadership may include:","helping coworkers stay on schedule and safe",["ignoring the crew","taking all breaks","hiding the plan"],"Leaders support the team.")
H("682.d.1.F",4,"A team member who finishes early and offers to help others is:","contributing to the team's success",["wasting time","breaking rules","showing off"],"Teamwork improves outcomes.")
H("682.d.1.G",3,"When working on an overhead cable run, a technician should use a:","stable ladder rated for the work",["wobbly chair","stack of boxes","desk on wheels"],"Proper ladders prevent falls.")
H("682.d.1.G",4,"Before handling fiber-optic cable ends, a technician should wear:","safety glasses",["sunglasses only","earmuffs","no protection"],"Fiber shards can injure eyes.")
H("682.d.1.H",3,"Using a coworker's login to access company data without permission is:","unethical and may be illegal",["harmless","encouraged","required"],"Unauthorized access breaks policy and law.")
H("682.d.1.H",4,"A technician working on a client's network sees confidential files. The ethical choice is to:","not open or share them",["read them for fun","copy them","sell them"],"Confidentiality must be kept.")
H("682.d.1.I",3,"A project schedule helps a team by showing:","what must be done and by when",["who won a game","what music is playing","lunch choices"],"Schedules coordinate work.")
H("682.d.1.I",4,"If a cabling job will take two days, the team should plan tasks in:","logical order with time for testing",["random order","reverse order only","no order"],"Order and testing time prevent rework.")
H("682.d.2.A",3,"To learn about a job as a network installer, a student could:","interview someone who does that job",["watch a cartoon","play a game","guess"],"Interviews give direct information.")
H("682.d.2.A",4,"Information about a job's wages and outlook can be found from:","the Bureau of Labor Statistics",["a rumor","a joke website","an advertisement for sneakers"],"BLS publishes job data.")
H("682.d.2.B",3,"A career plan should include:","goals and the steps to reach them",["only wishes","random ideas","nothing"],"Plans connect goals to actions.")
H("682.d.2.B",4,"Adding a certification to a plan helps show:","progress toward a specific job qualification",["a lack of direction","wasted time","a change of subject"],"Certifications are milestones.")
H("682.d.2.C",3,"Which description fits a strong resume for a job application?","accurate, neat and free of errors",["messy","exaggerated","handwritten in pencil"],"Resumes should be correct.")
H("682.d.2.C",4,"When applying for a telecom job, tailor your resume by:","emphasizing skills related to the posting",["listing every job you ever wanted","using a long paragraph","hiding your contact data"],"Tailoring improves match.")
H("682.d.3.A",3,"When a customer reports 'the internet is down,' a technician should:","ask questions to learn what exactly is not working",["assume the cause","hang up","change the router at once"],"Questions define the problem.")
H("682.d.3.A",4,"In a written network change request, the writer should state the:","reason for the change and the expected effect",["writer's hobbies","office color","lunch plans"],"Requests explain purpose and impact.")
H("682.d.3.B",3,"A work order for a new cable run might include the:","location and type of cable to install",["customer's favorite movie","technician's age","holiday schedule"],"Specifics guide the work.")
H("682.d.3.B",4,"Closing out a work order means:","recording completion and any issues found",["throwing it away","hiding it","ignoring it"],"Closure documents the result.")
H("682.d.3.C",3,"Materials for a cabling job are estimated by:","measuring distances and counting connectors",["guessing wildly","skipping the survey","asking for a bigger truck"],"Measurement leads to accurate estimates.")
H("682.d.3.C",4,"A job needs 300 feet of cable at $0.40 per foot and 20 connectors at $0.75 each. What is the material cost?","$135",["$120","$150","$115"],"120 + 15 = 135.")
H("682.d.3.D",3,"A wiring chart used by installers shows:","which wires go to which pins",["employee names","pay rates","car models"],"Charts show connections.")
H("682.d.3.D",4,"Interpreting a diagram incorrectly during installation could cause:","a network connection that does not work",["a faster network","fewer costs","more security"],"Errors lead to faults.")
H("682.d.4.A",3,"Analyzing a network starts with identifying its:","devices, cables and connections",["paint colors","chairs","clocks"],"Analysis starts with components.")
H("682.d.4.A",4,"Mapping which devices connect to which switch ports is useful for:","troubleshooting and planning changes",["decorating","scheduling meals","choosing names"],"Maps support management.")
H("682.d.4.B",3,"A small office with five computers and a printer would most likely use a:","single LAN with one switch",["global WAN","satellite network only","dozens of routers"],"Small needs call for simple designs.")
H("682.d.4.B",4,"A building with heavy electrical equipment may need:","shielded cable to reduce interference",["no cable","thinner cable","decorative cable"],"Shielding limits noise.")
H("682.d.4.C",3,"A company wants employees at two offices to share files securely. A suitable solution is a:","virtual private network (VPN)",["radio","telegraph","typewriter"],"VPNs link sites securely.")
H("682.d.4.C",4,"Scenario-based problems ask you to choose a network solution that fits the:","requirements and constraints given",["lowest price only","most colors","most devices owned"],"Solutions must fit the scenario.")
H("682.d.5.A",3,"Before installing a network, written plans should include a:","diagram of the layout",["lunch list","vacation request","costume"],"Diagrams guide installation.")
H("682.d.5.A",4,"A site survey before a network install helps identify:","obstacles and the best equipment locations",["menu choices","team nicknames","office slogans"],"Surveys reveal practical constraints.")
H("682.d.5.B",3,"Extreme dust in a server room can lead to:","overheating of equipment",["cooler parts","faster speeds","longer cables"],"Dust blocks airflow.")
H("682.d.5.B",4,"Why is humidity control important for network equipment?","too much causes corrosion and too little causes static",["it improves music","it paints walls","it makes cables longer"],"Both extremes can harm electronics.")
H("682.d.5.C",3,"The port on a switch where a computer's cable plugs in is typically labeled:","Ethernet or RJ-45",["HDMI","VGA","audio"],"Ethernet ports accept RJ-45 plugs.")
H("682.d.5.C",4,"A device that joins two different networks and forwards traffic between them is a:","router",["keyboard","speaker","scanner"],"Routers connect networks.")
H("682.d.5.D",3,"An addressing scheme assigns each device a:","unique address on the network",["nickname","paint color","job title"],"Unique addresses avoid conflicts.")
H("682.d.5.D",4,"With a /24 subnet, how many bits identify the network portion?","24",["8","16","32"],"A /24 uses 24 network bits.")
H("682.d.5.E",3,"A tool used to find where a cable is broken is a:","time-domain reflectometer or cable tester",["spoon","paintbrush","calculator only"],"Testers locate cable faults.")
H("682.d.5.E",4,"A tool for checking whether a cable end is wired to standard is a:","wire map tester",["tape measure","power drill","level"],"Wire map testers verify pin order.")
H("682.d.5.F",3,"Vendor documents that describe fixes for known issues are called:","patch notes or release notes",["menus","brochures","newsletters"],"Release notes list fixes.")
H("682.d.5.F",4,"Why read vendor testing documents before upgrading a router?","to confirm the update is compatible and safe",["to waste time","to avoid the upgrade forever","to find a coupon"],"Documentation guards against surprises.")
H("682.d.5.G",3,"Being aware of backup procedures means knowing:","what gets backed up and how often",["the CEO's lunch","the vending prices","the parking map"],"Procedures define backup scope and timing.")
H("682.d.5.G",4,"Storing backup tapes in a locked, fireproof safe protects them from:","theft and fire",["boredom","traffic","noise"],"Storage practices protect backup media.")
H("682.d.5.H",3,"The cable most associated with lower cost and easy installation in offices is:","unshielded twisted pair",["coaxial from a satellite","glass fiber","phone cord"],"UTP is cheap and flexible.")
H("682.d.5.H",4,"A cable best suited for very long, high-speed runs between buildings is:","fiber-optic cable",["flat patch cord","speaker wire","extension cord"],"Fiber carries data far at high speed.")
H("682.d.5.I",3,"Network performance can be reduced by:","outdated equipment and heavy traffic",["new equipment","low use","short cables"],"Old gear and congestion slow networks.")
H("682.d.5.I",4,"Adding a second access point in a large office may improve:","wireless coverage and capacity",["paper supply","parking","lighting"],"More access points spread the load.")
H("682.d.5.J",3,"Staying aware of new telecommunications technology means:","reading about changes in the industry",["avoiding news","ignoring trends","deleting emails"],"Awareness keeps skills current.")
H("682.d.5.J",4,"A technician hears that a new wireless standard has launched. A good move is to:","study its features and where it fits",["ignore it","laugh","delete all notes"],"Learning prepares you for change.")
H("682.d.6.A",3,"Before mixing old and new network equipment, a technician should check:","whether the devices are compatible",["the colors","the logos","the box sizes"],"Compatibility prevents failures.")
H("682.d.6.A",4,"Cat5e cable cannot support the highest speeds that Cat6a can. This is a:","cabling limitation",["software update","paint issue","font issue"],"Cable category limits speed.")
H("682.d.6.B",3,"An address like 192.168.1.20 is an example of:","an IPv4 address",["a phone number","a street address","a web page"],"IPv4 addresses use four numbers.")
H("682.d.6.B",4,"Putting a lab network and an office network on different subnets:","keeps their traffic separate",["merges all traffic","removes addresses","slows power"],"Subnets isolate groups.")
H("682.d.6.C",3,"When installing data connectors, the technician should follow the:","wiring standard, such as T568B",["alphabet","phone book","recipe"],"Standards ensure consistent wiring.")
H("682.d.6.C",4,"Which tool strips the outer jacket from a network cable?","a cable stripper",["a hammer","a ruler","a saw"],"Strippers remove jackets without nicking wires.")
H("682.d.6.D",3,"After attaching a connector to a cable, the technician should:","test the cable before using it",["throw it away","paint it","hide it"],"Testing confirms a good connection.")
H("682.d.6.D",4,"Connecting a patch cable between a wall jack and a computer completes the:","path to the network",["lunch order","power supply","screen display"],"The patch cable links device and jack.")
H("682.d.6.E",3,"A link light on a network port that stays off usually indicates:","no connection is detected",["a fast network","a printing job","a happy user"],"No link light means no signal.")
H("682.d.6.E",4,"Blinking lights on a switch port typically show:","data activity",["a power cut","a missing cable","a broken screen"],"Blinking indicates traffic.")
H("682.d.6.F",3,"Troubleshooting should follow a:","systematic approach",["random approach","guessing approach","skipping approach"],"A method avoids missed steps.")
H("682.d.6.F",4,"If all users lose access but the problem is not at their desks, the fault is probably:","a shared device or the internet link",["each user's mouse","each chair","each monitor"],"Shared failures point to shared parts.")
H("682.d.6.G",3,"Once a problem's cause is found, the next step is to:","choose and apply the best fix",["ignore the cause","guess again","blame someone"],"Corrective action follows diagnosis.")
H("682.d.6.G",4,"After applying a fix, a technician should:","verify that the problem is resolved",["leave quickly","hide the issue","skip documentation"],"Verification confirms the fix.")
H("682.d.6.H",3,"Organizing network files into folders by department helps users:","find and manage data more easily",["lose files","slow the drive","avoid sharing"],"Hierarchies improve organization.")
H("682.d.6.H",4,"Setting folder permissions so only one team can edit a folder protects:","the integrity of the team's data",["the monitor","the room","the speaker"],"Permissions control changes.")
H("682.d.7.A",3,"A security threat to an information system could be:","malware or unauthorized access",["a new chair","a sunny day","a quiet hallway"],"Threats harm systems or data.")
H("682.d.7.A",4,"Assessing security threats begins with identifying the:","assets that need protection",["office decorations","lunch breaks","parking spaces"],"You must know what to protect.")
H("682.d.7.B",3,"A common problem on a data network is:","unauthorized users trying to gain access",["too many windows","too much quiet","too short a cable"],"Access control is a core concern.")
H("682.d.7.B",4,"Weak passwords create a security need for:","password policies and multi-factor sign-in",["more paint","longer breaks","new chairs"],"Policies and extra factors reduce risk.")
H("682.d.7.C",3,"Using someone else's network without permission is considered:","unethical and often illegal",["a harmless game","a service","a requirement"],"Unauthorized use is wrongdoing.")
H("682.d.7.C",4,"Downloading and sharing paid music or movies without permission is called:","online piracy",["file backup","cloud storage","email"],"Piracy violates copyright.")
H("682.d.7.D",3,"The right to control who sees your personal data is called:","privacy",["publicity","speed","bandwidth"],"Privacy protects personal information.")
H("682.d.7.D",4,"A debate over how much the government should monitor communications involves balancing security and:","privacy rights",["screen size","cable color","font choice"],"This tension is central to policy.")
H("682.d.7.E",3,"A network security plan should be:","written down and shared with those responsible",["kept secret from everyone","never updated","lost"],"Written plans guide action.")
H("682.d.7.E",4,"Implementing a security plan includes training users on:","safe practices such as spotting phishing emails",["new wallpaper","game scores","office decor"],"Users are part of security.")
H("682.d.7.F",3,"A firewall helps secure a network by:","filtering traffic according to rules",["storing files","printing pages","cooling devices"],"Firewalls allow or block traffic.")
H("682.d.7.F",4,"An intrusion detection system watches the network and:","alerts staff to suspicious activity",["prints invoices","adds RAM","paints walls"],"IDS tools detect threats.")
H("682.d.8.A",3,"When pulling cable through a ceiling, a technician should avoid:","touching power lines and unsupported ceiling tiles",["wearing gloves","using a ladder","turning on a light"],"Ceilings can hide hazards.")
H("682.d.8.A",4,"Which safety item should be worn when drilling into a wall to run cable?","eye protection",["a scarf","slippers","a watch"],"Debris can injure eyes.")
H("682.d.8.B",3,"Old network equipment like routers and batteries should be:","recycled through an approved electronics program",["tossed in the trash","left outside","burned"],"E-waste needs proper disposal.")
H("682.d.8.B",4,"The document that explains how to handle a hazardous material safely is the:","Safety Data Sheet",["menu","brochure","receipt"],"SDS provides handling details.")
H("682.d.9.A",3,"Recovery plans for a telecom center should say what to do if:","power or a major link fails",["a lunch is late","a chair breaks","a pen runs out"],"Plans cover major outages.")
H("682.d.9.A",4,"A recovery plan should be tested by:","practicing the steps before a real emergency",["never reading it","hiding it","ignoring drills"],"Testing finds gaps.")
H("682.d.9.B",3,"Replacing worn cables before they fail is part of:","preventive maintenance",["guesswork","neglect","sales"],"Preventive work avoids failures.")
H("682.d.9.B",4,"A preventive maintenance schedule for a telecom closet might include:","regular inspections and cleaning of equipment",["leaving doors open","adding clutter","unplugging devices"],"Routine checks catch problems early.")

B.balance()
